#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0403 expect=violation domain=BW
#note "The mirror of -valid_phase_start_anchored-BW and the sharpest form of sheet issue #130's move (M3-D25, Fix #311): BWRPENDY carries -5, which is exactly the number the SHIPPED end-anchored Rule cell computed (BWENDTC 2020-01-15 minus SJENDTC 2020-01-20 within RPHASE P1). Under the guidance-anchored operation - reference SJSTDTC, reference_extreme min - the expected value is 14, so the end-anchored number is now REPORTED; before the move this record was silent and the conformant 14 fired. The two fixtures pin the swap in both directions. ⚠ ONE SJ STAGE ON PURPOSE: Match_Datasets joins SJ on (USUBJID, RPHASE), so N stages in a phase multiply each BW record into N joined rows and the finding COUNT with it - measured here, 2 SJ stages gave 2 findings for a single BW row. The count-bearing fixture therefore declares one stage; -valid_phase_start_anchored-BW keeps two, where a noViolation verdict is immune to the multiplicity and the earliest-vs-latest choice is still pinned. ⚠ Offset-0 arithmetic, EC-47 parked: offset RPRFDY is never applied (the column lives in TP, unreachable across the two-hop DM.RPATHCD bridge), and no dataset here declares TP, RPATHCD or RPRFDY. Re-check when EC-47 lands."
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 BWRPENDY=-5
dataset BW class=FINDINGS label="Body Weight"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col BWSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col RPHASE   type=Char label="Repro Phase"
col BWENDTC  type=Char label="End Date/Time of Observation"
col BWRPENDY type=Num  label="Repro Phase Day of End of Observation"
---
S1 | BW | 001 | 1 | P1 | 2020-01-15 | -5
---

dataset SJ class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Subject Repro Stages"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SJSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col RPHASE  type=Char label="Repro Phase"
col RSTAGE  type=Char label="Repro Stage"
col SJSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Repro Stage"
col SJENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Repro Stage"
---
S1 | SJ | 001 | 1 | P1 | STAGE1 | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-20
---
